        "original_id": "bbcecef3-0cb7-5253-8b28-1583a93151a5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lewis Gilbert, Lois Chiles, Michael Lonsdale, Corinne Cléry, Richard Kiel, Catherine Serre, Nicaise Jean Louis\n- Films: Moonraker, The Spy Who Loved Me, Inspector Gadget, Le gendarme et les gendarmettes\n- Roles: Jaws, Countess Labinsky, Drax Girl\n- Topics: James Bond franchise\n\nFacts:\n- Richard Kiel was an American actor, voice artist, and comedian born on September 13, 1939, and he later became best known for playing Jaws in the James Bond franchise.\n- Richard Kiel portrayed Jaws in The Spy Who Loved Me in 1977.\n- Moonraker was released in 1979, was directed as the third and final series entry by Lewis Gilbert, and co-starred Lois Chiles, Michael Lonsdale, Corinne Cléry, and Richard Kiel.\n- Richard Kiel portrayed Jaws again in Moonraker in 1979.\n- Catherine Serre appeared in Moonraker as Countess Labinsky, one of the “perfect” human specimens in Drax's master race.\n- Catherine Serre also appeared in Le gendarme et les gendarmettes alongside Nicaise Jean Louis, who was another Drax Girl from Moonraker.\n- Richard Kiel made a tongue-in-cheek cameo lampooning Jaws in Inspector Gadget in 1999.\n- Richard Kiel died on September 10, 2014.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
